1. Border Width & Direction (The Base)
• No letter: Applies to all 4 sides.
• t, b, l, r: Top, Bottom, Left, Right.
• x, y: Horizontal (left/right) or Vertical (top/bottom).

Tailwind Class      What it does                  CSS Equivalent
border              1px border on all sides       border-width: 1px;
border-2            2px border on all sides       border-width: 2px;
border-0            Removes all borders           border-width: 0px;
border-t            1px border on the top         border-top-width: 1px;
border-b-2          2px border on the bottom      border-bottom-width: 2px;
border-l            1px border on the left        border-left-width: 1px;
border-r-4          4px border on the right       border-right-width: 4px;
border-x            1px border on left & right    border-left: 1px; border-right: 1px;
border-y-0          Removes top & bottom borders  border-top: 0px; border-bottom: 0px;

2. The Responsive Prefix (sm:, lg:, xl:)

Breakpoint Prefix      When it activates                  Device
(No prefix)            Always active (Mobile First)       Mobile phones
sm:                    Screens 640px and wider            Large phones / Small tablets
md:                    Screens 768px and wider            Tablets (iPad portrait)
lg:                    Screens 1024px and wider           Laptops / iPad landscape
xl:                    Screens 1280px and wider            Widescreen Desktop Monitors


——  border-t: "By default (on mobile), put a 1px border on the Top to separate me from the panel above me."
——  border-zinc-200: "Make that border light gray."
——  lg:border-t-0: "Wait! If the screen stretches to Laptop size (lg:), remove that top border (-0), because the panels are no longer stacked vertically."
——  lg:border-l: "Instead, on Laptop sizes, add a 1px border on the Left to separate me from the panel that is now sitting horizontally next to me."

——  Border Color: border-white, border-zinc-200, border-white/20 (for transparent glass).
—— Border Style: border-solid (default), border-dashed (great for "Drag and Drop" upload zones), or border-dotted.
